==English==
[[Image:Toluene chemical structure.png|thumb|Chemical structure of toluene]]

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|de|Toluin}}, from {{m|de|Tolu}} ({{m|en|Tolú}}) where it was first distilled.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɒl.juː.iːn/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɑl.ju.in/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-toluene.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|organic compound}} A [[colourless]], [[inflammable]] [[liquid]] [[hydrocarbon]], [[methyl]][[benzene]], CH<sub>3</sub>.C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>, used as a [[solvent]], in [[high-octane]] [[fuel]]s and in the production of many [[chemical]] [[compound]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=w:Ocean Vuong|title=w:On Earth We're Briefly Gorgeous|publisher=Jonathan Cape|pages=79–80|passage=The salon is also a kitchen where, in the back rooms, our women squat on the floor over huge woks that pop and sizzle over electric burners, cauldrons of phở simmer and steam up the cramped spaces with aromas of cloves, cinnamon, ginger, mint, and cardamom mixing with formaldehyde, '''toluene''', acetone, Pine-Sol, and bleach.}}

